Without using my final two wishes, I did ascend that Valkyrie.  This is 
my first ascension not using the tiles (instead using the console 
version), first ascension since coming back to nethack after almost two 
years off, and third ascension overall (both previous were Valks).  Time, 
I think, to move on to a different class.  (Which, of course, was the 
idea until I got sick of dying as wizards/tourists and decided to play "a 
short valkyrie game...")

The details:

The start of the game was fairly common Valk bash-and-grab.  Then one of 
the wands in Sokoban turned out to be a wand of wishing.  I stared in 
surprise when engrave-ID'ing tells me "You may wish for an object."  The 
wand was 0:3, too.  I got 2 scrolls of charging out of the deal and 
finished Soko to see what it would give me.  Once I saw the amulet level, 
I wished up an AK fitting that; GDSM and a Cloak of Protection, Speed 
Boots, and GoPower.  Found a helm of brilliance just lying on the ground 
in the mines, and a tourist bones provided a Hawaiian shirt.  Enchanted 
the armor a bit.  

Made a lot of trips back and forth to minetown buying protection and sac-
festing (lawful altar).  Got Mjollnir, had Excalibur already.  On the 
last trip I accidentally angered the watch, and the watch-captain 
provided me with a silver saber.  I enchanted it up (had to redo after 
meeting a Disenchanter) and twoweaponed it and Excalibur most of the game.

Found a ring of conflict and a ring of levitation.  ID'd most of my stash 
with blessed identify.  Wished up a ring of free action, a magic marker, 
and scrolls of genocide, reverse-geno'd nurses.  Having unholy water and 
holy water made my life a lot easier.  Got rid of L and h, then ;, though 
next time I think I'll leave ; and get rid of Disenchanters/
Rustmonsters.  Tamed a grey dragon at the castle.

Between nurse dancing and blessed *healing, I was up to nearly 300HP 
before waking Rodney.  I also dug out the paths and marked the Vibrating 
Square before waking him, and quaffed some Gain Level, getting me up to 
XP 19 and HP 304.  Woke Rodney, instadeath'd him with Orcus's wand.  
Another random enemy, I think a demon, provided me with a second wand of 
death.  

Dragon ate a chameleon corpse, became a feline of some type; forget which 
now.  Found a poly-trap and whistled her back to being a dragon -- red 
this time.  In the sanctum, she died fairly quickly, but I didn't see 
what did it.  Cursed Gain level after getting the amulet, naming 
it,checking it.  Mysterious Force didn't bother me until I got up about 
seven levels, and I got it twice in a row and had to repeat most of 
Gehennom.  I was not pleased.

The run after escaping the Valley of the Dead was easy.  Rodney only 
bothered me twice in the dungeon proper; once at Medusa, once around 
Dlvl8.  the Medusa time, he took a few shots -- the wand missed him -- 
that nearly killed me on Astral.

The planes were easy -- XyZZy's suggestion of forgotten spells plus ?oGD 
made them a cinch.  Rested once in a steam vortex on air when my HP got 
low on air.  Levitated across water to the general area of the portal and 
found the bubble easily. On Astral, Pestilence was to my immediate left, 
so I went that way first.  /oD'd him, the altar wasn't right.  On my way 
out, he got close to me, and both /oD were drained.  I was losing HP fast 
(got down to 142 even with the blessed unihorn).

Desperation, I zapped Pestilence with a /oTele and recharged the wands.  
Ate a blessed tin of nurse I made in Hell.  Went up the middle, where 
Death was.  Teleported him away once, then just killed him.  When I got 
in the middle temple, a giant went to flee...

So I sac'd the amulet:

